{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_361607669#3_840144869","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is dedicated to electronics/e-waste recycling and directly discusses key challenges in recovering precious metals: crude dismantling in developing countries recovers much less gold, improper recovery exposes workers to hazardous substances, only a small share of devices reaches recyclers, and global metal recovery rates from e-waste are low.","learned":"Material-recovery challenges include low collection/recycling rates, inefficient recovery of precious metals, worker exposure to hazardous substances during improper recovery, and especially poor recovery in crude developing-country recycling operations."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1644","reason":"This query is producing strong evidence on valuable-material recovery and separation challenges, a key aspect of e-waste recycling, so continue for more grade-3 results."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1644"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_186084585#3_358401323","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1644","rank":2,"snippet":"waste Recycling Business Next What Business Research Team \" , \"segment\": \"Especially mobile devices, televisions, and computer devices are experiencing fast growth across the world. With increasing purchasing power and the rising trend of disposable income, the sale of these electronic devices is increasing continuously. In addition, the new product launches with updated features and additional services are attracting the customers to upgrade their old products with new products. This has reduced the lifespan of these devices to about 3-4 years. Thus, this is adding more and more e-waste at a tremendous rate. Therefore, the ongoing sale of electronics products provides a lucrative environment for e-waste management in the coming years. Why E-waste Recycling is Important? First of all, e-waste contains a huge amount of <cover>precious metals. And we can use those metals after the recovery from the scrap. Recycling e-waste </cover>helps to manage solid waste effectively.\" , \"start_char\": 1818.000000 , \"title\": \"How to Start E-waste Recycling Business in India - NextWhatBusiness\" , \"url\": \"https://nextwhatbusiness.com/e-waste-recycling-business/\" }"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"32/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_186084585#3_358401323","relevance":2,"reason":"The document is a business guide for starting an e-waste recycling business in India rather than a dedicated explanation of recycling challenges. It provides some supporting evidence that rapid electronics sales, frequent upgrades, short device lifespans, and growing e-waste volumes create pressure for e-waste management, and that precious metals need recovery from scrap.","learned":"Growing electronics consumption, frequent product upgrades, and shortened device lifespans increase e-waste volumes; e-waste also contains recoverable precious metals, making recovery an important but operationally significant issue."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1644","reason":"The current query has already produced strong evidence on precious-metal recovery and may yield more documents focused on material recovery challenges, so continue to the next result."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1644"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_186084585#4_358402905","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1644","rank":3,"snippet":"India E-waste Recycling Industry Potential in India Why E-waste Recycling is Important? Licenses & Permission for E-waste Recycling Business in India E-waste Recycling Business Model Investment for E-waste Recycling Business in India 10 Steps for Starting E-waste Recycling Business Next What Business Research Team \" , \"segment\": \"Therefore, the ongoing sale of electronics products provides a lucrative environment for e-waste management in the coming years. Why E-waste Recycling is Important? First of all, e-waste contains a huge amount of <cover>precious metals. And we can use those metals after the recovery from the scrap. Recycling e-waste </cover>helps to manage solid waste effectively. Actually, old electronic devices contain toxic substances such as lead, mercury, cadmium, and chromium. And these are tremendously harmful to the environment. Therefore, proper processing of e-waste is essential. Nowadays, e-waste contributes to more than 70% of the environmental pollution. And only recycling of e-waste can reduce environmental pollution.\" , \"start_char\": 2362.000000 , \"title\": \"How to Start E-waste Recycling Business in India - NextWhatBusiness\" , \"url\": \""}}
