{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_458289946#12_496656725","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is dedicated to electronic waste in China and directly supports key e-waste recycling challenges: widespread manual informal dismantling, severe lead and dioxin exposure in residents, higher miscarriage rates, high childhood blood lead levels, contamination of agricultural areas, soil and sediment pollution, and dietary heavy-metal intake through rice, vegetables, and water.","learned":"Informal e-waste recycling can create severe community-wide health and environmental impacts, including lead/dioxin exposure, reproductive harms, child blood-lead elevation, agricultural contamination, and heavy-metal intake through food and water."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1648","reason":"The current query has been the most productive source of grade-3 evidence on key e-waste recycling challenges, including informal-sector dominance, unsafe dismantling, hazardous exposure, environmental contamination, export incentives, and weak regulation."}}
